virglrenderer: no NULL dereference when a bound shader has no variant

What: vrend_sync_shader_io (the shader key of the stage before and after) and the
early link of VIRGL_CCMD_LINK_SHADER read sub_ctx->shaders[x]->current without a
check. A selector has no current variant after its TGSI failed to translate, and
the decoder keeps taking CREATE_OBJECT commands; the next shader created for a
neighbouring stage then crashed QEMU (the whole VM) on a NULL pointer. Now the
missing variant simply gives no clip/cull/colour/fs info for the key and is
skipped by the early link.
Why: a guest app could kill the VM with one command stream. Found by
Tests/virgl/fuzz-cmd-stream.c within seconds; the same input crashes the
unpatched tree (vrend_sync_shader_io).
Upstream: upstream bug, upstreamable as is; not sent.
Tests: the crash input replays clean (fuzz corpus); Tests/virgl/fuzz-cmd-stream.sh.
